    "top_frame": "The Pirates scored six runs in one inning and Pittsburgh never let them back into it.",
    "what_this_means": "This was a game decided by inning five, when Pittsburgh's offense exploded and the Giants never recovered from the deficit. The pitching held up its end. Landen Roupp struck out eight in four innings. But the rest of the team couldn't answer. Heliot Ramos was the only lineup piece who showed up, collecting two hits, but two hits don't win games when you're down ten. The offense left three on base in the sixth, when they might have clawed back. Instead, they struck out seven times total and went home early. This is what 15-24 looks like: one part bad luck, two parts self-inflicted damage, and zero margin for error when the pitching falters. Inconsistency doesn't build winning streaks.",
